{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559368-missing-purviews-or-what-new-purviews-do-we-want-need","id":559368,"title":"Missing Purviews!!! Or what new Purviews do we Want/Need?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-18T07:47:19-07:00","id":559368,"title":"Missing Purviews!!! Or what new Purviews do we Want/Need?","content":"I like the 16 general Purviews in the main book. The Additions of Frost, Stars, and Illusion, in later supplements were welcomed. However some divine powers seem to be missing.<br /> <br /> Among those I think we need/want are.....<br /> <br /> <b>A) Passion</b> Sure the Epic socials allow you to manipulate your emotional connections to others, but they don't allow you to simply cause one mortal to fall in love with another. Or lust. Or hate.<br /> <br /> A <b>Passion Purview</b> would cover things like, creating emotional bonds between individuals and groups, raising or lowering the passions of a community, changing the nature of passions or at least for the express themselves in the world. The highest levels could remove a passion from the world for a time or create a new passion!<br /> <br /> <b>B) Forge</b> The Smiths of the Gods are a widespread phenomenon. A Purview that covers crafts and technology is needed. the Atlantean Purview <b>Scire</b> would suggest some of the powers that would fit this purview. This a power that deals with technology would fit the scions of Wayland the Smith, Hephestus, or Shango in his role as God of Truck Drivers (yes Shago is the God of truck Drivers and worshiped as such in several nations).<br /> <br /> <b>C) Language/Communication</b> This purview would cover Language, communication, knowledge, and symbols, important mythic catagories. <b>Scire</b> mentioned above has some ideas for this purview. At lower levels in would allow the enhancement or blocking of communication and learning., the gift of tongues, and the ability to decode/encode information. Higher levels could remove knowledge or even whole languages from the world for a time.<br /> <br /> <b>D) Music/Harmony</b> Just as we have the <b>Chaos</b> purview for divine disorder we need a purview of divine order. As Music is the oldest and most emotive metaphore of divine order it would be deeply tied to this purview.<br /> <br /> More later, times up.<br /> <br /> What are your ides?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-18-2015, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T08:39:54-07:00","id":559411,"title":"","content":"You could technically lump Passion into Chaos...but I suppose it already has enough with all the weird stuff in there.<br /> <br /> Language I think is better served as epic INT boons<br /> <br /> Don't they usually counter Chaos with Law?<br /> <br /> Some other stuff they were missing; Time (there ARE time gods, even if they're notorious for just doing their job), Dream (there are dream gods too, yet they scattered all powers related to them across multiple purviews),<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T12:56:49-07:00","id":559718,"title":"","content":"Time powers, like stop time, slow time, speed up time, move super-fast via time, travel in time.. that's all <i>very much</i> a product of 1900s fiction and relatively recent understanding of how time/space works. Ancient gods of &quot;Time&quot; are really more like calendar gods, or gods of the seasons, or gods of entropy. They don't freeze things in time. The nearest you'd come is to how sometimes there are magical places where a day passes in a thousand years, or vice versa. There's just not a lot to work with unless you bring in modern superhero type powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T18:45:33-07:00","id":560176,"title":"","content":"Maybe some aging, youthen-ing, immortality add ons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:44:23-07:00","id":560362,"title":"","content":"I don't think there was ever a city/metropolis purview was there? That would be a pretty fun purview, giving you power over the flow of a city.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind seeing some modern purviews like technology or industry too as facets of being a modern god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:16:06-07:00","id":560402,"title":"","content":"I honestly think the whole idea of Purviews really needs to bugger off. It's kinda cool, but it ended up not working out in concept. They became Divine Disciplines instead of categories of power. There are hundreds of different things to be &quot;a god of&quot;.. which is a concept that's very Greco-Roman, anyway. Odin wasn't the God of X, Y and Z, he was ODIN. Sure, he did death, but he also did other stuff. It's the Greeks that gave us this idea of one God for one (or five) things. Most everyone else just had Gods, and didn't pigeon hole them into specific roles. <br /> <br /> A much more elegant solution would be clouds of powers with loose themes that can be stitched together to make whatever kind of deity you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:08:33-07:00","id":560716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559368-missing-purviews-or-what-new-purviews-do-we-want-need?p=559411#post559411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could technically lump Passion into Chaos...but I suppose it already has enough with all the weird stuff in there.<br /> <br /> Language I think is better served as epic INT boons<br /> <br /> Don't they usually counter Chaos with Law?<br /> <br /> Some other stuff they were missing; Time (there ARE time gods, even if they're notorious for just doing their job), Dream (there are dream gods too, yet they scattered all powers related to them across multiple purviews),</div> </div> </div> </div>The <b>Stars</b> Purview covers time. It's detailed in the Yazatas Book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:10:42-07:00","id":560717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559368-missing-purviews-or-what-new-purviews-do-we-want-need?p=560362#post560362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there was ever a city/metropolis purview was there? That would be a pretty fun purview, giving you power over the flow of a city.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind seeing some modern purviews like technology or industry too as facets of being a modern god.</div> </div> </div> </div>The God of the City is an ancient idea. The Romans Worshiped Cloaca Goddess of the Sewers, so the idea of Gods who watch over civic infrastructure is an ancient one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:12:13-07:00","id":560718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559368-missing-purviews-or-what-new-purviews-do-we-want-need?p=560402#post560402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly think the whole idea of Purviews really needs to bugger off. It's kinda cool, but it ended up not working out in concept. They became Divine Disciplines instead of categories of power. There are hundreds of different things to be &quot;a god of&quot;.. which is a concept that's very Greco-Roman, anyway. Odin wasn't the God of X, Y and Z, he was ODIN. Sure, he did death, but he also did other stuff. It's the Greeks that gave us this idea of one God for one (or five) things. Most everyone else just had Gods, and didn't pigeon hole them into specific roles.<br /> <br /> A much more elegant solution would be clouds of powers with loose themes that can be stitched together to make whatever kind of deity you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has a certain logic. But unless they make a serious change in the game system, we seem stuck with purviews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:43:01-07:00","id":560910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559368-missing-purviews-or-what-new-purviews-do-we-want-need?p=560718#post560718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That has a certain logic. But unless they make a serious change in the game system, we seem stuck with purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the serious changes they have been making so far in the fundamental underpinings of the game, I'm sure that godly powers will be comodified in a completely different way, whether or not the word &quot;Purview&quot; is used. I doubt we will see the Discipline/Arcanoi/Etc. system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:02:34-07:00","id":560941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559368-missing-purviews-or-what-new-purviews-do-we-want-need?p=560716#post560716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <b>Stars</b> Purview covers time. It's detailed in the Yazatas Book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stars should probably go away. While there are some very cool myths to be found related to Stars, there are so many dramatic differences between those myths that every Stars purview becomes a strange grab bag of powers or a very narrow slice of one or two cultures. Navigation has been the closest thing to a front runner for Stars, but even that has issues sharing design space with Psychopomp.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T18:22:49-07:00","id":561434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559368-missing-purviews-or-what-new-purviews-do-we-want-need?p=560941#post560941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stars should probably go away. While there are some very cool myths to be found related to Stars, there are so many dramatic differences between those myths that every Stars purview becomes a strange grab bag of powers or a very narrow slice of one or two cultures. Navigation has been the closest thing to a front runner for Stars, but even that has issues sharing design space with Psychopomp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I had Time and Stars overlap a bit, because some of the power in Stars were very good for a Time Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T23:54:56-07:00","id":561639,"title":"","content":"While I can't think of any Purviews off the top of my head that needed to be added (except maybe Craft?), I do kinda wish they were a lot more impressive and encompassing. What we got were basically situational Disciplines with extremely schizophrenic power placements and limited effects. A character with divine power over fire had to be closely approaching apotheosis just to start a fire (Fire 7: Inferno, Legend 8) without already being near one (or, you know, carrying a Bic.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/938-bigbad","name":"BigBad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T16:23:50-07:00","id":562318,"title":"","content":"As someone who's adapted several mythologies and magical traditions for multiple game systems, I can say that the relation between the source material and the gameable adaptation is always a bit like the relation between a cow and a meatloaf. Scion is no exception, but... after you've slaughtered and butchered the cow, selected the cuts of meat, ground them, added seasonings and other ingredients, patted it into shape and baked it, you should hope it at least still tastes like beef. If the meatloaf still manages to be cow-shaped, that's a bonus. Scion has it extra-difficult because it takes a cow, a pig, a chicken, and an iguana, mixes them all together -- but at the end, people still want the meatloaves to retain their taste.<br /> <br /> I am not sure the Purview system was the right approach. It's what we have until 2nd ed. comes out, though, and it's what Astromancer asked about, so that's what I'll discuss.<br /> <br /> Forge is indeed the most egregious lack from the Purview list, though I would rather call it Artifice: Smith-gods aren't the only mythic artisans (and Craft is already taken for an Ability).<br /> <br /> Other than that, my biggest wish would be to give Mystery and Prophecy the axe and make them Boons in a combined Purview of divination and knowledge. Call it Oracle, maybe. The various divinatory spells such as Ariadne's Thread go in Oracle as well.<br /> <br /> More later, maybe.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T11:41:24-07:00","id":563185,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking. We're missing two more perviews...<br /> <br /> <b>E) Inspiration</b> The gods bless humanity with insight and creative talent. Muses in the Greek myths, as well as Apollo. Brigit is the fire in the head. Odin among other gods inspired poets. Several Hind and Chinese gods inspired artists and crafts folk. An Inspiration Purview would be a good one.<br /> <br /> <b>F) Wealth</b> Gods of Wealth are common in many traditions. Blessing of riches aren't easily granted in the present system, and it is a common mythic theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:35:54-07:00","id":563295,"title":"","content":"The lack of those two Purviews really has a lot to do with game-play, not myth. Sure, it's great to be able to inspire mortals and grant them riches. But how does that come up in a game where mortals don't really matter? How does it affect you, as adventure-having heroes/demigods/gods? <br /> <br /> Look at Norse, Egyptian and (to a lesser degree) Aztec mythology where the gods are busy with their own stuff, generally ignoring humanity in favor of doing crazy things with other gods and monsters. There's not a lot of riches being handed out or inspiration given. That's something that matters to the worshippers, not the ones being worshipped, and in Scion you're playing on the second team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T11:11:00-07:00","id":564329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559368-missing-purviews-or-what-new-purviews-do-we-want-need?p=563295#post563295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of those two Purviews really has a lot to do with game-play, not myth. Sure, it's great to be able to inspire mortals and grant them riches. But how does that come up in a game where mortals don't really matter? How does it affect you, as adventure-having heroes/demigods/gods?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps by blessing a mortal with wealth, say a budding Edison or Tessla, clean energy sources displace dirtier ones and threaten a Titanic plot to destroy the World or Humanity. Similarly, inspired mortals can change the world. They can promote the values of the gods. Mortals can define fate, give the mortals inspiration and they'll tell Fate her place.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T11:23:53-07:00","id":564348,"title":"","content":"We have Purview for Justice, Guardian, and War, I think we need <b>G) Authority</b> as well. The King/Lord government Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:44:10-07:00","id":564942,"title":"","content":"Justice, Guardian, and War have lots of reason to be three different purviews, but they could all be part of the same purview as well. Justice didn't deal as much with the concept of Order as much as it did with punishing others based on the subjective laws of whichever pantheon happened to apply it. Really the &quot;Authority&quot; purview seems like it's contained in Justice. Guardian and War both seem like two sides of the same coin: Conflict. You are either attacking or defending, but you're still dealing with conflict in one way or another. Guardian needed more sealing powers and warding powers rather than defensive combat buffs. Especially since War has both offensive and defensive buffs in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T22:15:07-07:00","id":568802,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a Spirit Purview? The Japanese weren't the only culture to imagine a rich, varied and omnipresent spirit world. Shamanism is an aspect of so many mythic heroes that it should receive more support. Psychopomp covers the &quot;Travel To Other World&quot; part, and other parts might fit into other Purviews, but I think it's important enough in mythology to be pulled into a Purview of its own. Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:27:19-07:00","id":569229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559368-missing-purviews-or-what-new-purviews-do-we-want-need?p=568802#post568802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps a Spirit Purview? The Japanese weren't the only culture to imagine a rich, varied and omnipresent spirit world. Shamanism is an aspect of so many mythic heroes that it should receive more support. Psychopomp covers the &quot;Travel To Other World&quot; part, and other parts might fit into other Purviews, but I think it's important enough in mythology to be pulled into a Purview of its own. Dean Shomshak</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've got something there. <b>Death</b> covers ghosts, but ghosts are only a minority of spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T09:06:42-07:00","id":569294,"title":"","content":"It could be handled as a part of existing Purviews, just add a &quot;Talk to (X PURVIEW) Spirits&quot;, Hopefully not so much in a &quot;Summon Monster I-IX&quot; fashion. Arguably still a problem. Of course, gods of fire should be able to talk to fire spirits, but there are definitely some pantheons where gods should be able to talk to every kind of spirit and it seems unfair (and prohibitive under the Relic Purview access system) to ask them to invest in a little bit of every Sphere to get all the those abilities.<br /> <br /> So, more (semi-)redundant Boon profusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:22:46-07:00","id":569375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559368-missing-purviews-or-what-new-purviews-do-we-want-need?p=559411#post559411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could technically lump Passion into Chaos...but I suppose it already has enough with all the weird stuff in there.<br /> <br /> Language I think is better served as epic INT boons<br /> <br /> Don't they usually counter Chaos with Law?<br /> <br /> Some other stuff they were missing; Time (there ARE time gods, even if they're notorious for just doing their job), Dream (there are dream gods too, yet they scattered all powers related to them across multiple purviews),</div> </div> </div> </div>/lurk While I definitely see where you're coming from with dream, I used that as 'proof' that dream gods just weren't potent enough to manifest as Greater (legend 12) gods. My Somnus and Morpheus write-ups were still completely badass and I regret that my player's never got a chance to face the devious bastards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}